PianoUsbHost is new code for UniXNU-piano (BSD-2-Clause-Patent, LICENSE). Levels 1 and 2: a read-only survey; level 5: host mode with
our own minimal xHCI probe; level 6: Apple's AppleUSBXHCI on our nub (path A1). What it takes from other work, and from where:

UniXNU-piano (this repository), BSD-2-Clause-Patent:
  package/PianoAudio/PianoAudio.cpp (sha256 cb0499f7fa02dec2919101843c70a1d3d7b9eed389c77625ac032782321f6a8a): the kext's shape (probe
    gate on the boot argument, a survey thread, the post-mortem stage word, MMIO pages mapped on demand and loaded with an explicit ldr,
    one summary property), re-written for this driver; its decodePin / pullName copied into this namespace.
  package/PianoAudio/tests/audio_host.cpp (sha256 dfe2b7d81ac2cbe4a0633bf4441107c192a352cb448e0df663a74e0709298833): the register-model
    harness (Soc, CHECK), re-used in tests/usbhost_host.cpp (and its CHECK in the other two tests).
  package/PianoDwc3/PianoUsbHw.h (sha256 3c07c280fdd57d4c2cff068bca75f59b6d9a4c1f3b6302a2b77f0c3de97240d6): included, not copied (GCC
    clock and power-domain offsets, QSCRATCH, the repeater's PPID, the DWC3 base, SPI 133, the SMMU and stream 0x40); the core-clocked
    rule is PianoDwc3's clocksOn(), extended by the sleep clock for the QSCRATCH store gate.
  package/PianoDwc3/SmmuStream.h (sha256 8f566938f259730d15407aa2d84abb3f6ec3b06c7bf3dabaef78c7e7fbb930a3): included, not copied (level
