QcomDwc3 (unixnu-research/QcomDwc3, main e4efe95c903a737e0f5955e5b50a8fb4d2a7d718; BSD-2-Clause-Patent except QcomEusb2Phy.h and
QcomQmpUsb3.h, which are GPL-2.0-only and were not read for this). QcomDwc3.cpp (sha256
4b29c0aa6ed893c9b11b1c129795a2c1ddd9bf44e39ad79e2294de61113250f2):
  smmuIdentity(): adapted into SmmuIdentity.h (BSD-2-Clause-Patent, attribution kept there): the level-1 identity table (T0SZ 28, 1 GiB
    blocks from 2 GiB, attribute 0 write-back, inner shareable, AF, unprivileged read/write) and the context bank words (CBA2R, CBAR,
    TCR2, TCR, TTBR0/1, MAIR0/1, SCTLR M/TRE/AFE/CFRE/ASIDPNE); split into plan/apply, an existing exact entry redirected instead of
    refused, TLBIALL instead of TLBIASID, non-zero TLB values.
  QcomDwc3Nub and enterHost(): facts and shape for PianoUsbHostNub, written anew: an IODeviceMemory of 0x8000 bytes at the core as
    memory 0, the name usb-host0, a 4-byte bus-number 0, interrupt source 0 as getInterruptType / registerInterrupt / unregister /
    enable / disable with a level type, the nub attached to the platform expert and registered, the controller started on it, the
    nub terminated to stop it; hostStats()'s count of IOUSBHostDevice services with idVendor/idProduct. Its armcpu_spi_mask (not in
    our kernel) is replaced by the distributor's set/clear-enable bits. NOT used: its QcomDwc3Xhci subclass (three vtable overrides
    of AppleUSBXHCI: path A2, the owner's decision), its PHY sequences.
  setCoreRole(): the role change shape (a core soft reset, PRTCAPDIR, the PHY suspend bits) as one witness besides Linux.
  QcomUcsi.h (sha256 5c688feeddd335ddc3e2f06baa9909fc7fbd1712285b6216d23bb85a60cf94b3) is the UCSI client a later level derives from
  (docs/drivers/usb-host.md sections 4 and 9).

